        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes the linter, adding MDN urls for features that include the <code class=\"notranslate\">@@</code> prefix.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Ensures that <code class=\"notranslate\">@@iterator</code> etc gets an <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn_url</code> automatically.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Triggered via <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4233820489\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29441\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29441/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29441\">#29441</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29454",
            "title": "fix(lint): add MDN urls for features with `@@` prefix",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T14:55:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-10T21:23:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1152698?u=5ce323090a48b425ec70128365c96809699959f7&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds partial implementation flags and notes for <code class=\"notranslate\">align-self</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">justify-self</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">place-self</code> for all browsers, when they apply to absolutely positioned elements.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tested this in Safari, Firefox, and Chrome, and discussed with Mozilla engineers <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/dshin-moz/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/dshin-moz\">@dshin-moz</a> and <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/emilio/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/emilio\">@emilio</a>.<br>\nMy understanding is that there's a missing piece in all browsers where you can't just apply the above properties and expect them to work on their own. They also require a non-auto <code class=\"notranslate\">inset</code> value.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test case: <a href=\"https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965</a></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..lK13a1xglMcFSdmZkR12jqhl238QTJkHmaCfAzkg2oI\"><img width=\"859\" height=\"685\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..lK13a1xglMcFSdmZkR12jqhl238QTJkHmaCfAzkg2oI\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 685px;; aspect-ratio: 859 / 685; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The red box should be centered in the gray box.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n  .parent { position: absolute; inset: 20vmin; background: gray; }\n  .child { position: absolute; width: 50%; aspect-ratio: 1; background: red; justify-self: center; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;parent&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;child&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">style</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n  .<span class=\"pl-c1\">parent</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">position</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> absolute; <span class=\"pl-c1\">inset</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">20<span class=\"pl-smi\">vmin</span></span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">background</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> gray; }\n  .<span class=\"pl-c1\">child</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">position</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> absolute; <span class=\"pl-c1\">width</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">50<span class=\"pl-smi\">%</span></span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">aspect-ratio</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">background</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> red; <span class=\"pl-c1\">justify-self</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> center; }\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">style</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">class</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">parent</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">class</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">child</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adding <code class=\"notranslate\">inset:0;</code> on the child element makes it work.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not entirely sure I'm reading the spec correctly though, and the placement of auto-inset abspos elements may actually be correct. But, WPT seems to show browser differences in this area at least: <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Firefox bug that was filed as a result of my discussion with Mozilla engineers: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174</a></li>\n<li>Related Chromium issue: <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29342",
            "title": "Chromium partially supports `{align,justify,place}-self` with absolute positioning",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-04T06:27:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-25T14:14:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "captainbrosset",
                "url": "https://github.com/captainbrosset"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 supports the <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> pseudo-element, which allows custom styling to be applied to browser search results; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We already have BCD for <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code>, however, you can combine <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> with the <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> pseudo-class to style the currently-highlighted search term on the page. This currently doesn't have any BCD, so I am using this PR to add <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm assuming it makes sense to put Chrome 144 down for this as well, as previously, there was no context in which <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> was supported. However, you might have other opinions on this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also thought about putting <code class=\"notranslate\">\"partial_implementation\": \"true\"</code> for this, but then again, <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> is fully supported in the context it is supported in. It just isn't supported in other contexts.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29543.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4329766971\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29543\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29543/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29543\">#29543</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28882",
            "title": "Chrome 144 :current support",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-30T19:48:25.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-21T18:28:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is updates to add details to cover Safari support for documentId and parentDocumentId. More information on changes see the related content PR. (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3818058205\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42786\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42786/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42786\">mdn/content#42786</a>)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28341.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3575616610\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\">#28341</a><br>\nRelated content changes in (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3818058205\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42786\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42786/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42786\">mdn/content#42786</a>)</p>",
